{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Summary\n\nrebar documents a relocatable ticket store as a supported feature, then bypasses its own\nresolver in dozens of shipped code paths, each assuming the store sits at\n`repo_root/.tickets-tracker`. Any deployment that relocates the store — which the deployed MCP\nserver does — breaks in those paths, with errors that name a path the operator never configured.\n\n## The contract that is being ignored\n\n`src/rebar/config.py:138-156` (`tracker_dir()`) is explicit: the env override\n`REBAR_TRACKER_DIR` 'wins verbatim'; otherwise the configured `tracker.dir` applies, where 'an\nabsolute value relocates the store (EV-3b)'. Relocation is a FEATURE, not an edge case.\n\n## Observed failure (reported from a live Copilot session)\n\n    bridge_status -> command_failed, exit 1\n    \"cannot read bridge status: cannot read local environment id from\n     /var/gerrit/site/mcp-code/.tickets-tracker/.env-id: [Errno 2] No such file or directory\"\n\nThe deployed server sets `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR=/var/gerrit/site/mcp-tickets`. The store is there and\nis healthy — 2763 tickets are readable through the same server.\n\nREPRODUCED LOCALLY (see the RCA comment): with a store relocated outside the repo root and\n`REBAR_TRACKER_DIR` set to it, `rebar list` succeeds (rc=0) while `rebar bridge status` fails\nnaming `<repo_root>/.tickets-tracker/.env-id`. The control arm is what makes the experiment\ndiscriminating: same env, same store, same repo — only the resolver-bypassing path fails.\n\n## Root cause (CONFIRMED, runtime)\n\n`src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/last_pass.py:89` composes\n`repo_root / \".tickets-tracker\" / \".env-id\"`; the caller `_lib_ops.py:288` passes the repo root,\nnever the resolved tracker. The sibling constant at `:35` has the same defect for the last-pass\ndetail file (`:170` read, `:268` write).\n\nAttributed to `b69c-5787-81b8-4052` (`antivirus-talkative-beauceron`) via introducing commit\n`fe5a447061cde`. `config.tracker_dir()` already carried the relocation contract verbatim at that\ncommit's PARENT, so this is a `plan_defect` (a new composition written past an existing seam),\nnot a regression and not an unmet obligation.\n\n## Triage of the 77 occurrences\n\nEvery `.tickets-tracker` hit in `src/rebar/` was triaged. **13 are defects; 64 are legitimate.**\n\n- **13 DEFECT** — compose a store path bypassing the resolver (enumerated as AC1-AC13 below).\n- **4 LEGITIMATE-DEFAULT** — the default name inside a resolver: `config.py:154`,\n  `_config_schema.py:631`, `_engine_support/reads.py:120`, `runtime.py:44`\n  (`_DEFAULT_TRACKER_DIR`, the default inside the reconciler's own `_resolve_tracker_dir`, which\n  DOES honour an absolute `tracker.dir`).\n- **5 LEGITIMATE-BOUNDARY** — compose a path that is correctly not the local configured store:\n  `_snapshot/ticket_view.py:73` and `_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py:586` build paths inside a\n  temp/snapshot directory the code itself just created; `llm/config.py:317` adds a denylist\n  SUPERSET beside a real `tracker_dir()` call (denying more is safe); `_commands/fsck.py:253`\n  builds the default name deliberately AS the comparison subject for a\n  \"tracker.dir changed without migrating\" warning.\n- **55 PROSE** — docstrings, comments, argparse help, error/recovery text.\n\nNote: the `# tickets-boundary-ok` marker is NOT evidence of correctness today — 7 of the 13\ndefects carry it. Nothing enforces it, so it has been applied as a rubber stamp. AC14's gate\nmakes the marker mean something by requiring a reason and rejecting unmarked compositions.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\nEach confirmed sibling is its own criterion (Step 7 class review), ordered by MCP reachability.\n\n**Tier 1 — MCP-reachable and mutating**\n\n- [ ] AC1: `_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_store.py:601` (`load_binding_store`) resolves the\n      binding read/write root through the resolver.\n- [ ] AC2: `_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile.py:318` resolves the `prev_snapshot.json` root\n      (and therefore `ctx.tracker_dir`, consumed by `run_differs.py:434`).\n- [ ] AC3: `_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile.py:456` `check_store_compat` validates the\n      CONFIGURED store, so the fail-closed precheck cannot be defeated by relocation.\n- [ ] AC4: `_engine/rebar_reconciler/dispatch_one.py:321` writes `BRIDGE_ALERT` events into the\n      configured store rather than materializing a shadow store at the repo root.\n- [ ] AC5: `_engine/rebar_reconciler/git_adapter.py:75` + its consumer\n      `reconcile_helpers.py:234` stage the binding-store commit-back from the configured store.\n- [ ] AC6: `_bridge_runner.py:180` passes the RESOLVED tracker to the delivery subprocess\n      instead of a relative `.tickets-tracker` interpreted against `cwd`.\n- [ ] AC7: `_engine/rebar_reconciler/projects_store.py:47` reads and writes the sync mapping in\n      the configured store, so the write and `_lib_ops`' commit target the same directory.\n\n**Tier 2 — MCP-reachable, read/diagnostic**\n\n- [ ] AC8: `_engine/rebar_reconciler/last_pass.py:35` resolves the last-pass detail file.\n- [ ] AC9: `_engine/rebar_reconciler/last_pass.py:89` reads `.env-id` from the configured store.\n- [ ] AC10: `_engine/rebar_reconciler/inbound_translate.py:165` honours the `tracker.dir` config\n      key, not only `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR`.\n- [ ] AC11: `_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py:239` (reconcile-check) loads local tickets\n      from the configured store.\n\n**Tier 3 — CLI-only**\n\n- [ ] AC12: `_engine_support/bridge_fsck.py:663` CLI fallback honours the `tracker.dir` key.\n- [ ] AC13: `_engine/rebar_reconciler/__main__.py:508` dry-run enumeration errors rather than\n      silently reporting an empty store when relocated.\n\n**Cross-cutting**\n\n- [ ] AC14: A `make lint` gate rejects NEW store-path composition from the hardcoded literal in\n      `src/`, enforcing the existing `# tickets-boundary-ok` convention with a MANDATORY reason\n      (matching the `# raw-git-ok:` gate's vocabulary). The 64 legitimate occurrences pass.\n- [ ] AC15: A regression test exercises `bridge_status` with `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR` pointing\n      OUTSIDE the repo root, and fails if the hardcoded composition is reintroduced\n      (mutation-checked).\n- [ ] AC16: `bridge_status` succeeds unchanged in the DEFAULT in-tree layout (no\n      `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR`, default `tracker.dir`) — no regression for the common case.\n\n## Definition of Done\n\n- [ ] DD1: AC1-AC13 hold, each site routed through `config.tracker_dir()` or the reconciler's\n      already-resolved `ReconcilerSettings.tracker_dir`.\n      Verify: `python scripts/check_tickets_boundary.py`\n- [ ] DD2: AC14's gate runs in `make lint` and is RED if any drained site regresses.\n      Verify: `make lint`\n- [ ] DD3: AC15's test is RED before the fix and GREEN after; re-introducing the hardcoded\n      path returns it to RED.\n      Verify: `pytest tests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_status_relocated_store.py`\n- [ ] DD4: No regression in the reconciler, bridge, snapshot, or store suites.\n      Verify: `pytest tests/interfaces/facades tests/unit/rebar_reconciler`\n- [ ] DD5: `make lint` and `make typecheck` clean.\n\n## Scope note\n\nThis ticket supersedes `cca6-3f7e-dd67-439f` (`addictive-snooty-wildcat`), whose AC1-AC5 cover\nonly AC8/AC9 here. Linked `duplicates`.\n\n- [ ] **LIVE VALIDATION — REQUIRED TO CLOSE.** `bridge_status` called through the deployed endpoint returns its status snapshot instead of the `.env-id` ENOENT.\n      Evidence must be OBSERVED against the deployed server at\n      `https://rebar.solutions.navateam.com/mcp` and recorded in a ticket comment naming\n      the tool(s) called, the arguments, and the actual response. A passing local test is\n      NOT sufficient, and neither is a merged change: the container must have redeployed\n      and served the call. This exists because a fix here was previously reported complete\n      on the strength of a merge while the deployed behaviour was still broken.\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1787860130663129001,"uuid":"bf511b4a-8fde-4b83-9e4e-86701b475d50"}